{"event_type":"review","id":"a8c3c988046fa35d2d2f8c3decddd150ad670bc65a4f6ba8dff936df3d4c28f7","occurred_at":"2026-11-14T20:48:01Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3942fdf405163c3933a763d4a3a4eccae7d2b7cb9ac1efb2b7e499e6be76ddd4","sha256":"3942fdf405163c3933a763d4a3a4eccae7d2b7cb9ac1efb2b7e499e6be76ddd4"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/62982b5ff4e06eb77f3bd25d268ad9336172818cbaf39b5ea834062137962c68","sha256":"62982b5ff4e06eb77f3bd25d268ad9336172818cbaf39b5ea834062137962c68"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3689c995398933efcf8bac35abe4c6b3405df42fe14d0f7a685c6a0b0ec1203d","sha256":"3689c995398933efcf8bac35abe4c6b3405df42fe14d0f7a685c6a0b0ec1203d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/538374390348c8010692fbc3cbda6dd1b93599072abd103c5f34158acfe2a124","sha256":"538374390348c8010692fbc3cbda6dd1b93599072abd103c5f34158acfe2a124"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0d0ad6f93a1f4d1d05f1380201a055265872061e8bea6f80681c42b1a61291fc","sha256":"0d0ad6f93a1f4d1d05f1380201a055265872061e8bea6f80681c42b1a61291fc"}],"attempt_id":"8a97254f45a82ca962a1a4e84ba256fa8dd7528d8cca83e71b173c1289d831a6:0:1","base":"bdbf8440eb1a33edac096f39d5710fcdf3a2f946","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"92ebf082bcc2b58ba8b38625e1763f388ad27d6f","body":"**Traverse installation script references transitively.**\n\nAt `src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts`, Line 172, only lifecycle commands can select other scripts. Consider `prepare: \"npm run setup\"` and `setup: \"npm run patch\"`. Installation executes the referenced scripts, but this helper retains `setup` without inspecting its command. ([docs.npmjs.com](https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v6/commands/npm-run-script/?v=true&utm_source=openai))\n\nIf only `patch` changes, `relevant()` drops that change and the metadata check succeeds. Dependencies produced by the previous patch command can then be reused. Traverse referenced scripts and their hooks until no new script names remain. Use a visited set to handle cycles.","id":"913e1ab5d163c21be6f9ee5eb3f789c2c9306a382da63e4b7c9c3ad85e4ba321","intervals":[[172,172]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Traverse installation script references transitively."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"92ebf082bcc2b58ba8b38625e1763f388ad27d6f","body":"**Compare binary lockfiles without UTF-8 decoding.**\n\nAt `src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts`, Line 159, every metadata file becomes a UTF-8 string, including `bun.lockb`, which is binary. UTF-8 decoding replaces invalid sequences, so different bytes such as `0x80` and `0x81` can become the same string. ([bun.sh](https://bun.sh/docs/pm/lockfile?utm_source=openai))\n\nLine 201 can then accept different lockfile bytes and allow reuse of a mismatched dependency tree. Read non-manifest metadata as `Buffer` values. Decode only files that require parsing.","id":"448a922aa061554d65561343ad0c51327a75afd5337a48e7b8689cf1b7533bd7","intervals":[[159,159]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Compare binary lockfiles without UTF-8 decoding."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"9af09a20b9b098fa428d74eab139a2d6fc215dfc","body":"**Reject checkout-owned Git paths by path component.**\n\nWith root `/repo` and PATH entry `/repo/..tools`, `relative(canonical, candidate)` returns `..tools/git`. This is a descendant path, not a parent traversal. ([nodejs.org](https://nodejs.org/api/path.html))\n\nThe prefix check accepts `/repo/..tools/git`. If that file is executable, `terminalGit` runs checkout-controlled code as trusted Git at `src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts:426-430`. The later inode check does not prevent this because it records the selected file itself.\n\nCheck for an exact `..` component or `..` followed by the platform separator. Reject descendant paths even when their first component starts with two dots.","id":"66a1b682750ec211dc2c378ebb31342788765f4ee88ae26d330182e268a0c57f","intervals":[[238,238]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject checkout-owned Git paths by path component."}],"head":"3005ab2216e0c48cc325a8f866db2ecec559a244","head_tree":"40cca612920bd0f60b7d7ded61025db433bf3a2a","input_scope":[{"blob":"92ebf082bcc2b58ba8b38625e1763f388ad27d6f","intervals":[[1,267]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts"},{"blob":"9af09a20b9b098fa428d74eab139a2d6fc215dfc","intervals":[[1,1119]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts"},{"blob":"fba6334e8f4f9e6615344f582d8ba9a5ef0cc123","intervals":[[1,1018]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressManyPlan.ts"}],"job_id":"8a97254f45a82ca962a1a4e84ba256fa8dd7528d8cca83e71b173c1289d831a6:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"92ebf082bcc2b58ba8b38625e1763f388ad27d6f","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"9af09a20b9b098fa428d74eab139a2d6fc215dfc","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"fba6334e8f4f9e6615344f582d8ba9a5ef0cc123","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressManyPlan.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/